# /lib/beacon/verbs -- the system tier of the presentation verb table
# (BEACON.md 7; docs/HALCYON.md 13.6 "obj interaction"). One rule per line:
#
#   <type> <label> <command template...>
#
# The menu on a presented object offers the labels for its type; choosing
# one runs the template with every `{}` replaced by the RESOLVED ref,
# single-quoted for ut (rc's rule: '' is the one escape) -- the command
# acts on exactly the ref the menu displayed. Types are BEACON.md 12.2's:
# path, pid, url, commit, user. Baked from usr/lib/beacon/verbs.default.

path   ls        ls -l {}
path   cat       cat {}
path   stat      stat {}
path   cd        cd {}
path   edit      nora {}
path   hexdump   hexdump {}
pid    kill      kill {}
url    fetch     wget {}
